00:02:25.677 --> 00:02:28.550
Yeah! Carol! [laughs]

00:02:28.593 --> 00:02:30.726
She's psyched.

00:02:30.769 --> 00:02:34.251
Branch, I love
that we're different.

00:02:34.294 --> 00:02:37.733
And I love you, Queen Poppy.

00:02:38.777 --> 00:02:41.084
I love you, too, Branch.

00:02:41.911 --> 00:02:44.130
Shall we?

00:02:47.264 --> 00:02:48.700
-Yeah! [whoops]
-Yes!

00:02:48.744 --> 00:02:52.530
-Now, that's a good connection!
-[laughs]

00:02:52.574 --> 00:02:55.533
POPPY: In the beginning,
we were divided.

00:02:55.577 --> 00:02:58.057
["The Other Side" by SZA
and Justin Timberlake playing]

00:02:58.101 --> 00:02:59.537
Our ancestors thought

00:02:59.581 --> 00:03:02.453
we were just too different
to get along.

00:03:02.497 --> 00:03:04.716
It turns out they were wrong.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.544
Very, very wrong.

00:03:06.588 --> 00:03:08.285
ANCESTOR TROLL:
We're sorry.

00:03:08.328 --> 00:03:10.592
POPPY: You have to be able
to listen to other voices,

00:03:10.635 --> 00:03:12.289
even when they don't
agree with you.

00:03:12.332 --> 00:03:14.378
-[Trolls sigh]
-[hands clap]

00:03:14.421 --> 00:03:16.380
They make us stronger,

00:03:16.423 --> 00:03:18.948
more creative, more inspired.

00:03:18.991 --> 00:03:22.081
So whether your song is
sad and heartfelt,

00:03:22.125 --> 00:03:24.301
loud and defiant,

00:03:24.344 --> 00:03:26.172
or warm and funky,

00:03:26.216 --> 00:03:28.871
or even if you're
a little bit of each,

00:03:28.914 --> 00:03:31.526
it's all these sounds
and all our differences

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:33.789
that make the world
a richer place.

00:03:33.832 --> 00:03:35.138
♪ On the other side...

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:37.967
Because you can't
harmonize alone.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:39.142
[Clampers laughs, chomps]

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:41.231
[blabbering]

00:03:41.274 --> 00:03:42.275
